## Frequently asked questions

### Do I need a separate AEO agency as well as ecommerce SEO?

No, most UK ecommerce stores do not need a separate AEO agency as well as ecommerce SEO. AI assistants draw on the same product pages, feeds, reviews and third-party sources that search engines use. Good ecommerce SEO covers most of that groundwork. A separate AI visibility audit is worth it when you need a measured baseline. It shows how often assistants mention, cite or recommend your store and which sources they rely on.

My guide to the [best AEO agencies](/blog/best-aeo-agencies/) compares UK options. It includes me and carries a disclosure.

### How much does ecommerce SEO cost?

Ecommerce SEO with me costs from £495 for a Shopify audit, from £750 for a WooCommerce audit and fix, from £1,500 for a Magento audit and from £1,500 per month on a retainer. I am not VAT-registered. The final price is quoted after the free 20-minute diagnosis.

### How do I compare SEO providers for an ecommerce website?

Compare SEO providers for an ecommerce website on four things: what the audit costs and covers, who does the implementation, how they handle your product data and feed, and how they report organic revenue rather than rankings alone. The questions in the AEO table above work for any ecommerce SEO provider.

